From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/52] feat(ui): the reviewer dock keeps to moving around and
 reviewing

The reviewer layout's dock had grown to fifteen controls, and the pages
took a panel down the left side of the canvas. Asked for less: the pages in
the dock as a pick-one, no renderer label, and import, export, comments and
the people behind one control, so the bar holds navigation and review and
the rest is one click further.

Desktop dock, in order: back, the canvas's name and id; Hand and Comment;
the zoom; the page picker (the page shown, opening the canvas's pages as a
pick-one menu); the faces of who is here, which open one menu: who is here,
the comments panel (its trigger wears a dot while threads are open),
import, export, share, the design panel, settings and your name. Seven
controls where there were fifteen.

No left panel in the reviewer layout: the Pages panel and its collapsed
island go, and the canvas takes the width back (the fits and floating
chrome no longer keep clear of it). Adding, renaming and ordering pages
stay with the full editor's Pages panel (the docked layout, or FULL_UI).
LayersPanel and PagesPanel lose the pages-only face they had for this
layout; PagesPanel is upstream's again.

The renderer label and its view option stay out of the dock's zoom
control; Settings > Appearance still picks the renderer, and the docked
layout's zoom pill still shows the label.

A phone's dock swaps its Pages sheet for the same picker (the icon alone);
its Comments button stays, the comments being a phone's main way to review.

Tests: reviewerLayoutBrowser checks what the dock leaves out, no left
panel, picking a page from the dock, and the menu's items, opening and
closing the comments from it; phoneReviewBrowser checks the picker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
